# Storybook wrappers for interactive state

When a story needs to exercise loading, success, or error **after a user
action** (file drop, submit, click), do not only pass a static
`makeInProgressState()` into the presentational component. Wrap it in a
`StoryWrapper` in the stories file that owns local state.

Type the story as `StoryFn<StoryWrapperProps>`, not `StoryFn<InnerProps>`.
`StoryWrapperProps` is a story control surface:

- `Pick` (or pass through) Inner props the story should still tweak.
- Replace callbacks and live state the wrapper owns (`onSubmit`, `status`)
  with story-only seeds such as `initialStatus`.

`Template` always mounts `StoryWrapper` so Default / Loading / Error share
the same interaction path. Story `args` are wrapper props; the wrapper maps
them onto Inner.

```tsx
interface StoryWrapperProps
  extends Pick<SomeComponentInnerProps, 'enableFullScreenDrop'> {
  initialStatus: APICallState<Result> | null;
}

const defaultProps: StoryWrapperProps = {
  enableFullScreenDrop: true,
  initialStatus: null,
};

const metadata: Meta = {
  title: 'SomeComponentInner',
  component: SomeComponentInner,
  args: defaultProps,
};
export default metadata;

const StoryWrapper: React.FunctionComponent<StoryWrapperProps> = React.memo(
  function StoryWrapper(props: StoryWrapperProps) {
    const { enableFullScreenDrop, initialStatus } = props;
    const [status, setStatus] = useState(initialStatus);

    const handleSubmit = useMemoizedCallback(async () => {
      setStatus(makeInProgressState());
      await delay(5000);
      setStatus(makeDoneState({ id: 'storybook-id' }));
    }, []);

    return (
      <SomeComponentInner
        enableFullScreenDrop={enableFullScreenDrop}
        onSubmit={handleSubmit}
        status={status}
      />
    );
  }
);

const Template: StoryFn<StoryWrapperProps> = (args) => (
  <StoryWrapper {...args} />
);

export const Default: StoryFn<StoryWrapperProps> = Template.bind({});

export const Loading: StoryFn<StoryWrapperProps> = Template.bind({});
Loading.args = { initialStatus: makeInProgressState() };
```

Keep the wrapper in the `.stories.tsx` file unless more than one story file
needs it.

If a callback does not mutate wrapper state, pass `makeFakeHandler` from
`lib/storybook.ts` instead of a local no-op.
